  "body": "QUESTIONABLE / PROJECTION. CHECK-040’s water, cure-compression and bond findings are folded into 048 in 648 new configurations. Original filed artifacts remain unchanged.\n\nAt 1 mm retained exterior water, all 432 R10–15 cases fail to float, including all-four endpoints and favorable interior-optimism bounds. Best all-four payload is −998.333 kg; best favorable bound is −998.280 kg. Neither 0.1 nor 1 mm is a measured retention limit. No bake, dry-gas or sorbent route earns an exterior wet-service reduction; material water stays separately accounted.\n\nIncluding cure compression in global/crimp demand reduces the multilayer R10 ISA bake endpoint from +124.262 to +118.695 kg; least set becomes G+Q+film usage .842794. Two previously floating marginal configurations lose every allowed set. CHECK-040’s original R15 optimistic all-four −1.821 kg case reproduces.\n\nThe 200°F source tests use AF163-2K .060 metal joints, EC-3924B and 50 psi. They do not qualify 2U .015 Be/honeycomb. Exact bond/process NFI is explicit. Thermal-table independent reproduction and all original qualifications remain open; installed-hull SF stays null.\n\n130,278 checks pass across 10,469 distinct points. All 43 CHECK-040 cure targets reproduce within .000684 kg. Package verifies 69 pins. The separate 030d register order is now active.",
